  "rulings": [
    {
      "comment": "Players can only respond once this spell has been cast and all its costs have been paid. No one can try to interfere with the creature you sacrificed to prevent you from casting this spell.",
      "oracle_id": "24227761-b50e-4b9e-93a2-e82d053b3e3d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must sacrifice exactly one creature to cast this spell; you can't cast it without sacrificing a creature, and you can't sacrifice additional creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "24227761-b50e-4b9e-93a2-e82d053b3e3d",
      "published_at": "2019-10-04",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Use the sacrificed creature's power as it last existed on the battlefield to determine how much damage Fling deals.",
      "oracle_id": "24227761-b50e-4b9e-93a2-e82d053b3e3d",
      "published_at": "2024-04-12",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The sacrificed creature\u2019s last known existence on the battlefield is checked to determine its power and its toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "6a5ce1b0-ac78-4a74-9eb7-4064e1687bf1",
      "published_at": "2010-06-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must sacrifice exactly one creature to cast this spell; you cannot cast it without sacrificing a creature, and you cannot sacrifice additional creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "6a5ce1b0-ac78-4a74-9eb7-4064e1687bf1",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Players can only respond once this spell has been cast and all its costs have been paid. No one can try to destroy the creature you sacrificed to prevent you from casting this spell.",
      "oracle_id": "6a5ce1b0-ac78-4a74-9eb7-4064e1687bf1",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Twincast can copy any instant or sorcery spell, not just one with targets.",
      "oracle_id": "8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the spell has damage divided as it was cast, the division can't be changed, although the targets receiving that damage still can. The same is true of spells that distribute counters.",
      "oracle_id": "8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The copy will have the same targets as the spell it's copying unless you choose new ones. You may change any number of the targets, including all of them or none of them. If, for one of the targets, you can't choose a new legal target, then it remains unchanged (even if the current target is illegal).",
      "oracle_id": "8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the spell that's copied is modal (that is, it says \"Choose one \u2014\" or the like), the copy will have the same mode. A different mode can't be chosen.",
      "oracle_id": "8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If the spell that's copied has an X whose value was determined as it was cast, the copy will have the same value of X.",
      "oracle_id": "8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The copy is created on the stack, so it's not \"cast.\" Abilities that trigger when a player casts a spell won't trigger. The copy will resolve before the original spell does.",
      "oracle_id": "8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can't choose to pay any alternative or additional costs for the copy. However, effects based on any alternative or additional costs that were paid for the original spell are copied as though those same costs were paid for the copy.",
      "oracle_id": "8f878efc-850f-43d2-a6fe-5ea8d1dd5afb",
      "published_at": "2021-03-19",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must sacrifice exactly one creature to cast this spell; you cannot cast it without sacrificing a creature, and you cannot sacrifice additional creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "84ca8d74-95ec-4a9c-8793-7a195ad28be9",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Players can only respond once this spell has been cast and all its costs have been paid. No one can try to destroy the creature you sacrificed to prevent you from casting this spell.",
      "oracle_id": "84ca8d74-95ec-4a9c-8793-7a195ad28be9",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "X is the power of the sacrificed creature as it last existed on the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "d33aa11b-011b-4d12-85a9-4f956153fb1d",
      "published_at": "2011-06-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You must sacrifice exactly one creature to cast this spell; you cannot cast it without sacrificing a creature, and you cannot sacrifice additional creatures.",
      "oracle_id": "d33aa11b-011b-4d12-85a9-4f956153fb1d",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Players can only respond once this spell has been cast and all its costs have been paid. No one can try to destroy the creature you sacrificed to prevent you from casting this spell.",
      "oracle_id": "d33aa11b-011b-4d12-85a9-4f956153fb1d",
      "published_at": "2013-04-15",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Although all the cards in The Brothers' War that create Powerstone tokens create a tapped Powerstone token, entering the battlefield tapped isn't part of the token's definition. Notably, if you create a token that is a copy of a Powerstone token, the token copy won't enter the battlefield tapped.",
      "oracle_id": "178828a5-c202-4503-9755-fc6bb2390209",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Powerstone tokens are a kind of predefined token. Each one has the artifact subtype \"Powerstone\" and the ability \"{T}: Add {C}. This mana can't be spent to cast a nonartifact spell.\"",
      "oracle_id": "178828a5-c202-4503-9755-fc6bb2390209",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You can use the {C} added by a Powerstone token on anything that isn't a nonartifact spell. This includes paying costs to activate abilities of both artifact and nonartifact permanents, paying ward costs, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "178828a5-c202-4503-9755-fc6bb2390209",
      "published_at": "2022-10-14",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If you control Mox Opal and one other artifact, then have a second Mox Opal enter the battlefield as your third artifact, you can't activate either one's mana ability before putting one into your graveyard due to the \u201clegend rule.\u201d",
      "oracle_id": "de2440de-e948-4811-903c-0bbe376ff64d",
      "published_at": "2020-08-07",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Any untapped creature you control can be tapped to pay a crew cost, even one that just came under your control.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Creatures that crew a Vehicle aren't attached to it or related in any other way. Effects that affect the Vehicle, such as by destroying it or giving it a +1/+1 counter, don't affect the creatures that crewed it.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Each Vehicle is printed with a power and toughness, but it's not a creature. If it becomes a creature (most likely through its crew ability), it will have that power and toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "For a Vehicle to be able to attack, it must be a creature as the declare attackers step begins, so the latest you can activate its crew ability to attack with it is during the beginning of combat step. For a Vehicle to be able to block, it must be a creature as the declare blockers step begins, so the latest you can activate its crew ability to block with it is during the declare attackers step. In either case, players may take actions after the crew ability resolves but before the Vehicle has been declared as an attacking or blocking creature.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a permanent becomes a copy of a Vehicle, the copy won't be a creature, even if the Vehicle it's copying has become an artifact creature.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If an effect causes a Vehicle to become an artifact creature with a specified power and toughness, that effect overwrites the Vehicle's printed power and toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a Vehicle becomes a creature, it behaves exactly like any other artifact creature. It can't attack unless you've controlled it continuously since your turn began, it can block if it's untapped, it can be tapped to pay a Vehicle's crew cost, and so on.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once a player announces that they are activating a crew ability, no player may take other actions until the ability has been paid for. Notably, players can't try to stop the ability by changing a creature's power or by removing or tapping a creature.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Vehicle is an artifact type, not a creature type. A Vehicle that's crewed won't normally have any creature type.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When a Vehicle becomes a creature, that doesn't count as having a creature enter the battlefield. The permanent was already on the battlefield; it only changed its types. Abilities that trigger whenever a creature enters the battlefield won't trigger.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may activate a crew ability of a Vehicle even if it's already an artifact creature. Doing so has no effect on the Vehicle. It doesn't change its power and toughness.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may tap more creatures than necessary to activate a crew ability.",
      "oracle_id": "f2c43b85-8c42-4b23-84c2-bec8d6230039",
      "published_at": "2017-09-29",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "It\u2019s the ability, not the counter that makes the creature an artifact. The creature remains an artifact even if the +1/+1 counter is removed.",
      "oracle_id": "1a8072c9-e2b8-4173-af88-ed0dd64d10fe",
      "published_at": "2007-09-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "If a token is exiled this way, it will cease to exist and won't return to the battlefield.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Once the exiled permanent returns, it's considered a new object with no relation to the object that it was. Auras attached to the exiled permanent will be put into their owners' graveyards. Equipment attached to the exiled permanent will become unattached and remain on the battlefield. Any counters on the exiled permanent will cease to exist.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "The returned card won't be the target of any spells or abilities that targeted it before. Any spells that don't target, such as Akroma's Vengeance, will still affect it.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "When an effect returns the exiled card \"under your control,\" you control it indefinitely after that. In a multiplayer game, if a player leaves the game, all cards that player owns leave as well. If you leave the game, any creatures you control from Cloudshift's effect are exiled.",
      "oracle_id": "6879f5ce-7a1b-4606-bad1-885779b0d456",
      "published_at": "2018-03-16",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "Becoming an artifact doesn't change what color(s) a permanent is.",
      "oracle_id": "f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af",
      "published_at": "2011-01-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    },
    {
      "comment": "You may target any permanent with the ability, including an artifact.",
      "oracle_id": "f4bdc551-c2eb-4a34-a3e3-b4a017c925af",
      "published_at": "2011-01-01",
      "source": "wotc"
    }
  ],
